prlimit of any process, through a Prlimit sysdep: a system whose kernel
reads and sets the resource limits of other processes implements it, and
prlimit asks it in one call, with the pid it was given. Without it prlimit
works on the calling process alone, as getrlimit and setrlimit do, and
fails with ENOSYS for any other, which is all mlibc's own could do. Meant
for upstream.

